1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,375
Cold Storage and the Frozen-Meat Trade

2
00:00:03,375 --> 00:00:07,196
On the 8th of June 1903, a
company called Cold Storage

3
00:00:07,276 --> 00:00:11,746
was registered in Singapore to
solve one very specific problem:

4
00:00:11,826 --> 00:00:14,780
there was no reliable way, in the tropics,

5
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:19,050
to keep a piece of meat cold
long enough to eat it safely.

6
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:23,118
Everything the company became
afterwards — the supermarkets,

7
00:00:23,198 --> 00:00:26,298
the ice cream, the dairy
farm, even a shopping

8
00:00:26,378 --> 00:00:30,250
mall on Orchard Road — grew
out of that one narrow need.

9
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:33,857
Cold Storage's first cargo,
imported chilled meat,

10
00:00:33,937 --> 00:00:38,723
poultry and dairy products from
Queensland, Australia, went into a

11
00:00:38,803 --> 00:00:43,375
400-tonne refrigeration facility
on a wharf at Keppel Harbour.

12
00:00:43,375 --> 00:00:48,820
The company opened its first retail
shop on the 24th of March 1905,

13
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:52,775
at the corner of Cuppage
Road and Orchard Road.

14
00:00:52,775 --> 00:00:55,767
It did not do well at
first: domestic servants,

15
00:00:55,847 --> 00:01:00,343
who did much of the everyday household
shopping for European families,

16
00:01:00,423 --> 00:01:03,741
largely avoided it, and the
company's early attempts

17
00:01:03,821 --> 00:01:07,271
at importing fresh fruit and
vegetables mostly spoiled

18
00:01:07,351 --> 00:01:10,750
on the sea journey before
they ever reached a shelf.

19
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:15,875
Business only recovered from
1909, under new management.

20
00:01:15,875 --> 00:01:19,474
The company kept building
on the same basic idea —

21
00:01:19,554 --> 00:01:23,600
controlled cold, delivered
reliably — well beyond meat.

22
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:27,361
In 1923 it opened a
small ice cream factory

23
00:01:27,441 --> 00:01:31,550
at Borneo Wharf under
the brand name Paradise.

24
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:36,204
In 1937 its managing director,
an Australian named Fred Heron,

25
00:01:36,284 --> 00:01:39,945
founded what the company
called the world's first

26
00:01:40,025 --> 00:01:44,144
tropical dairy farm, at Bukit
Timah: some 60 acres and,

27
00:01:44,224 --> 00:01:48,419
at its peak, around 800 cows,
producing pasteurised milk

28
00:01:48,499 --> 00:01:52,775
for a market that had never
had fresh local milk before.

29
00:01:52,775 --> 00:01:57,330
Paradise ice cream was relaunched
that same year under a new name,

30
00:01:57,410 --> 00:02:01,825
Magnolia — a brand that outlived
Cold Storage's own ownership of

31
00:02:01,905 --> 00:02:06,400
it and is still a familiar name
in Singapore supermarkets today.

32
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:11,252
In 1959, Cold Storage's Orchard
Road outlet became Singapore's

33
00:02:11,332 --> 00:02:15,468
first self-service supermarket,
a format almost every

34
00:02:15,548 --> 00:02:20,400
grocery shop on the island now
uses without a second thought.

35
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:24,410
By the early 1980s, Cold
Storage was successful enough

36
00:02:24,490 --> 00:02:28,125
to become a property
developer in its own right.

37
00:02:28,125 --> 00:02:32,281
In November 1983 the Cold
Storage Group opened Centrepoint,

38
00:02:32,361 --> 00:02:36,445
the shopping mall that still
stands on Orchard Road today,

39
00:02:36,525 --> 00:02:39,900
and moved its own flagship
supermarket into it.

40
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,846
For decades afterward,
"the Cold Storage at

41
00:02:42,926 --> 00:02:46,153
Centrepoint" was simply
where a certain kind of

42
00:02:46,233 --> 00:02:49,400
Singapore household did
its grocery shopping.

43
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:52,560
My own family was a
typical Chinese household,

44
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:56,082
and Christmas was a newer,
lighter occasion for us

45
00:02:56,162 --> 00:02:59,825
growing up — we celebrated,
but with different food.

46
00:02:59,825 --> 00:03:04,202
It was only after I married my
wife, whose family kept a bigger,

47
00:03:04,282 --> 00:03:09,286
more established Eurasian-style
Christmas built around particular dishes,

48
00:03:09,366 --> 00:03:12,500
that ham became part of
our own celebrations.

49
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:16,558
Every year before Christmas
we'd go to the Cold Storage

50
00:03:16,638 --> 00:03:20,700
on Orchard Road, behind
Centrepoint, to buy a raw ham.

51
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:24,839
The first time we brought home
one glazed in pineapple and honey,

52
00:03:24,919 --> 00:03:29,123
it was such a hit that it became
a fixture — and it's the specific

53
00:03:29,203 --> 00:03:33,666
memory that ties our family, in a
small way, to a company that started

54
00:03:33,746 --> 00:03:37,900
out solving a completely different
problem eighty years earlier.

55
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:42,150
Cold Storage's own ownership
changed more than once.

56
00:03:42,150 --> 00:03:45,895
In 1992, Dairy Farm
International — part of the

57
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:50,289
Jardine Matheson group —
bought Cold Storage Holdings'

58
00:03:50,369 --> 00:03:54,600
retail operations for 130
million Singapore dollars.

59
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:59,332
That arrangement lasted over
three decades, until March 2025,

60
00:03:59,412 --> 00:04:04,302
when DFI Retail Group sold its
entire Singapore food business —

61
00:04:04,382 --> 00:04:08,246
48 Cold Storage, CS Fresh
and Jason's Deli stores,

62
00:04:08,326 --> 00:04:13,137
41 Giant stores, and two
distribution centres — to Macrovalue,

63
00:04:13,217 --> 00:04:17,950
a Malaysian retail group, for
125 million Singapore dollars.

64
00:04:17,950 --> 00:04:23,168
Macrovalue's new owners promised
lower prices and more choices;

65
00:04:23,248 --> 00:04:28,125
the deal was expected to close
in the second half of 2025.

66
00:04:28,125 --> 00:04:33,198
Cold Storage is, if anything, more
visible today than it has ever been —

67
00:04:33,278 --> 00:04:36,848
a premium-priced alternative
sitting alongside NTUC

68
00:04:36,928 --> 00:04:40,999
FairPrice and Sheng Siong on
almost every shopping street,

69
00:04:41,079 --> 00:04:46,375
in neighbourhoods that have nothing
to do with its old European clientele.

70
00:04:46,375 --> 00:04:50,005
On a visit back to Singapore,
I stayed in Joo Chiat and

71
00:04:50,085 --> 00:04:53,783
was surprised to find a Cold
Storage branch right there,

72
00:04:53,863 --> 00:04:57,897
a short walk from the old
Peranakan shophouses — not the kind

73
00:04:57,977 --> 00:05:01,608
of address I'd have expected
for a brand that built its

74
00:05:01,688 --> 00:05:05,600
name on chilled Australian
mutton for colonial households.

75
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:09,925
It's pricier than the other chains,
and it's still there anyway.

76
00:05:09,925 --> 00:05:14,488
Why it matters today: most people
walking into a Cold Storage

77
00:05:14,568 --> 00:05:19,055
today are just doing their
weekly shopping, in a supermarket

78
00:05:19,135 --> 00:05:23,550
format the company itself
introduced to Singapore in 1959.

79
00:05:23,550 --> 00:05:28,124
Almost nobody buying a ham there
at Christmas is thinking about

80
00:05:28,204 --> 00:05:32,631
a 400-tonne refrigeration shed
on a wharf in 1903, or a dairy

81
00:05:32,711 --> 00:05:37,063
farm with 800 cows in Bukit
Timah, or the fact that the mall

82
00:05:37,143 --> 00:05:41,650
around them was built by the
grocer, not the other way round.
